## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical ability to design a DLT-based ingestion, including schema drift handling, per-tenant partitioning, and end-to-end quality checks in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Delta Live Tables (DLT)
- Data quality with expectations
- Schema drift tolerance
- Rollback/version control
- Lineage and monitoring

## Code Example
```python
import dlt

@dlt.table
def bronze_logs():
  return spark.read.parquet("s3://bucket/logs/")

@dlt.table
def silver_logs(bronze_logs):
  df = bronze_logs.filter("event_id IS NOT NULL")
  return df.select("tenant_id", "date", "event_id", "event_type", "payload")

@dlt.table
def gold_metrics(silver_logs):
  return silver_logs.groupBy("tenant_id").agg(count("event_id").alias("events"))
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle schema changes without breaking downstream dashboards?
- How would you monitor and alert on data quality failures in production?
